Bluetooth: L2CAP: defer security block while link encryption is pending

Base:     Linux 7.3 + ps5-linux-patches (linux.patch, "meower" branch)
File:     net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c
License:  GPL-2.0 (same as the file it modifies)

On the PS5 Pro MediaTek controller a bonded DualSense sends its HID control
L2CAP connection request (PSM 0x11) about 0.7 s before the controller reports
Encryption Change. Stock l2cap_connect() answers "Connection refused -
security block" and the DualSense disconnects (reason 0x13).

This change skips the immediate security block when the link is not yet
encrypted, a link key exists (key_type != 0xff) and the feature-mask exchange
is done, so the channel is not rejected while encryption is still being set up.
Without it the DualSense cannot connect on this hardware (verified with the
unmodified bluetooth.ko, see docs/test-results.md).

Security: the channel is answered "pending / authentication pending"
(BT_CONNECT2) and only reaches BT_CONFIG after the link is encrypted, for SSP
links; for non-SSP links behaviour is unchanged. Code review against Linux 7.3,
see docs/technical-analysis.md section 5. No negative test has been run.

Origin: not original work. This is the PS5 Linux community "encryption
pending" workaround, first published in WizGery/ps5-mediatek-fixes and later
taken into rmuxnet/ps5-linux-patches-1. If your linux.patch already contains
it, do not apply this patch.

Apply in a kernel tree that already has linux.patch applied:
    git apply 0002-bluetooth-l2cap-defer-security-block-while-encryption-pending.patch
---
--- a/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c
@@ -4127,6 +4127,12 @@
 
 	/* Check if the ACL is secure enough (if not SDP) */
 	if (psm != cpu_to_le16(L2CAP_PSM_SDP) &&
+            !test_bit(HCI_CONN_ENCRYPT, &conn->hcon->flags) &&
+            conn->hcon->key_type != 0xff &&
+            (conn->info_state & L2CAP_INFO_FEAT_MASK_REQ_DONE)) {
+                BT_DBG("conn %p encryption pending, deferring psm 0x%2.2x",
+                       conn, __le16_to_cpu(psm));
+        } else if (psm != cpu_to_le16(L2CAP_PSM_SDP) &&
 	    (!hci_conn_check_link_mode(conn->hcon) ||
 	    !l2cap_check_enc_key_size(conn->hcon, pchan))) {
 		conn->disc_reason = HCI_ERROR_AUTH_FAILURE;
